#nexus [SplitsTree6]

BEGIN SPLITSTREE6;
DIMENSIONS nDataNodes=11 nAlgorithms=8;
PROGRAM version='SplitsTree App (version 6.5.1-j8, built 27 Sep 2025)';
WORKFLOW creationDate='1759286087587'; [Wed Oct 01 11:34:47 JST 2025]
END; [SPLITSTREE6]

[
Methods:
Analysis was performed using SplitsTree App 6.0.0 (Huson and Bryant 2024).
The original input consisted of 36 taxa and a 36 x 36 distance matrix.
The Neighbor Net method (Bryant & Moulton 2004, Bryant & Huson 2023) was used (default options) so as to obtain 86 splits, cyclic.
The Razor Net method was used (default options, except Epsilon=0.001, MinDistance=0.1) so as to obtain 104 nodes and 120 edges.
The Network Pruning method (Hayamisu et al 2025) was used (default options) so as to obtain 104 nodes and 120 edges.
The Show Splits method was used (default options) so as to obtain a Split Network visualization.

References:
Bryant & Huson 2023: D. Bryant and DH Huson, NeighborNet- improved algorithms and implementation. Front. Bioinform. 3, 2023.
Bryant & Moulton 2004: D. Bryant and V. Moulton. Neighbor-net: An agglomerative method for the construction of phylogenetic networks. Molecular Biology and Evolution, 21(2):255– 265, 2004.
Hayamisu et al 2025: M. Hayamisu et al, in preparation, 2025.
Huson and Bryant 2024: D.H. Huson and D. Bryant. The SplitsTree App: interactive analysis and visualization using phylogenetic trees and networks. Nature Methods, 2024.
]

